<title>USA: Rykoff-Sexton arbitration resolved, sees no impact.</title>
<headline>Rykoff-Sexton arbitration resolved, sees no impact.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rykoff-Sexton Inc said Friday it concluded an arbitration proceeding which arose out of the October 1994 sale by Rykoff-Sexton of its subsidiary, Tone Brothers Inc, to Burns, Philp and Co Ltd affiliate Burns Philp Food Inc.</p>
<p>The company said the arbitration award, which is final and binding, is not material and will not impact Rykoff-Sexton's financial results.  </p>
<p>Rykoff-Sexton is a foodservice distribution company with sales of about $3.6 billion.</p>
<p>	     Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
